{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.B4MultiplicativeCumulant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B4MultiplicativeCumulant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BodyOrderCumulant"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor_barOdd_proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor_barOdd_proj","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L146-L151","doc":"**Bar-odd projection = `−h`.**  The (doubled) bar-odd projection\n`½(f_pn − f_pn^bar)` of the pn factor is `−h`, i.e. the projection is `−h/2` —\nthe radiated (Q_β-like) channel, not retained binding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor_barEven_proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor_barEven_proj","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L138-L144","doc":"**Bar-even projection = the Markov weight `z`.**  The (doubled) bar-even\nprojection `½(f_pn + f_pn^bar)` of the pn factor is `2z`, i.e. the projection is\n`z` — the retained binding part is exactly the pp/nn Markov weight, stripped of\nthe bar-odd `−h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor_bar_mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor_bar_mixed","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L132-L136","doc":"**The pn factor is bar-mixed** (I-par refined, not passed as stated): its bar\nimage differs from itself by `2h`, so it is bar-invariant iff `h = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactorBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactorBar","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L129-L130","doc":"The bar image of `twoPnFactor` under `z ↦ z, h ↦ −h`: `2z − (−h) = 2z + h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.twoPnFactor","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L125-L127","doc":"Twice the pn pair factor, `2·(z − h/2) = 2z − h`.  (Working with the doubled\nform keeps everything over a generic `CommRing` — no division needed.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_b4_nonvacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_b4_nonvacuous","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L103-L110","doc":"**Non-vacuity / contrast with the additive route.**  Concretely at\n`τ = 1, f = 0` the multiplicative 4-body cumulant is `3 ≠ 0`, whereas every\nadditive form (`fourthDiff_linear`, `fourthDiff_pairwise` in `BodyOrderCumulant`)\ngives `0` identically.  So the multiplicative binding is the structurally\ncorrect place to look for the missing ⁴He `b₄` — it is not orthogonal to the\n4-body channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.satBinding_b4_at_f_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.satBinding_b4_at_f_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L98-L101","doc":"The pure-saturation cumulant also vanishes at `f = 1` (`3 − 6 + 4 − 1 = 0`):\na constant per-nucleon factor carries no connected 4-body content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.satBinding_b4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.satBinding_b4","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L89-L96","doc":"**Pure-saturation cumulant** (drop the extensive `τ^A` growth, `τ = 1`).  The\nconnected 4-body part of `Bsat(A) = 1 − f^{C(A,2)}` is the explicit polynomial\n`3 − 6f + 4f³ − f⁶`.  This is the \"saturation ceiling\" the probe's headline sits\nagainst: it isolates how much connected 4-body content the *pair-count exponent*\n`C(A,2)` alone supplies, independent of the (weak) `τ^A` growth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_b4_at_f_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_b4_at_f_one","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L82-L87","doc":"**No coupling ⇒ no connected cumulant.**  At `f = 1` every saturation factor\n`1 − f^k` vanishes, so the multiplicative 4-body cumulant is `0`.  The connected\ncontent is generated *entirely* by the coupling `f ≠ 1`; there is no spurious\n4-body term from the extensive `τ^A` growth alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_b4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_b4","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L69-L80","doc":"**Closed form of the multiplicative connected 4-body cumulant.**  The 4th\nforward finite difference of the multiplicative binding sequence is\n`τ⁴(1−f⁶) − 4τ³(1−f³) + 6τ²(1−f)`.  This is the quantity the probe evaluates\n0-fit; the finite-difference extractor is the same `fourthDiff` proved in\n`BodyOrderCumulant` to annihilate ≤2-body content, so this is genuinely the\n*connected* 4-body part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_four","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_three","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_two","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding_zero","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.multBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.multBinding","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4MultiplicativeCumulant.lean#L49-L61","doc":"The **symmetric-cluster multiplicative binding** table\n`B(A) = τ^A · (1 − f^{C(A,2)})` for `A = 0,…,4`, with pair counts\n`C(A,2) = 0,0,1,3,6`.  (0/1-body: no pairs ⇒ `1 − f^0 = 0` ⇒ `B = 0`.)  This is\nthe symmetric idealisation of the framework binding\n`E₀ · τ_vac · (1 − ∏ f)`; the overall `E₀` scale is dropped (it cancels in the\nfraction-of-target headline the probe reports). ","signatureChunk":0}]}